\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.9}{\ignorespaces The selected data driven stress test results. The left column shows the weights at particle level and the fitted function. The middle column shows reconstruction level distributions, where the acceptance correction has already been performed. The result of the data driven stress test is shown in the right column. The upper row shows the lepton \ensuremath  {p_{\text  {T}}}\xspace  in the bulk region (\subref {fig:stress_test_data_bulk_lepton_pt_fct}, \subref {fig:stress_test_data_bulk_lepton_pt_reco}, \subref {fig:stress_test_data_bulk_lepton_pt_truth}), the middle row the \ensuremath  {m_\mathrm  {T}^{\min }(b\ell )}\xspace  in the search-like region (\subref {fig:stress_test_data_search_like_mtblmin_fct}, \subref {fig:stress_test_data_search_like_mtblmin_reco}, \subref {fig:stress_test_data_search_like_mtblmin_truth}), and the bottom row the \ensuremath  {m_{bW}^\mathrm  {minimax}}\xspace  in the hadronic \ensuremath  {W}\xspace  region (\subref {fig:stress_test_data_whad_minimax_fct}, \subref {fig:stress_test_data_whad_minimax_reco}, \subref {fig:stress_test_data_whad_minimax_truth}). Only statistical MC uncertainties are shown.}}{39}{figure.caption.94}\protected@file@percent }
